  <Document>
    <name>☁️ LIVE CLOUD COVER</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<h2>LIVE CLOUD COVER</h2><p><b>Data time:</b> 2026-09-26 18:21 UTC<br/><b>Source updated:</b> n/a (S3)<br/><b>Source version:</b> goes19-acmc-20260926-1821<br/><b>Processed:</b> 2026-09-26 02:27 PM EDT<br/><b>Status:</b> LIVE / CURRENT OBSERVATION (GOES-East 5-min scans)</p><p><b>Legend</b><br><img src="https://wyattleathorn7.github.io/great-lakes-live-environment/cloud_cover/legend.png?v=goes19-acmc-20260926-1821" width="600" alt="legend"><br>Cloud cover (%, OBSERVED neighborhood fraction from GOES-East: share of 2 km satellite pixels flagged cloudy around each point): <b>LOWEST 0 clear</b> transparent &rarr; thin cloud <b>dark-blue/blue/cyan</b> &rarr; <b>40 green</b> &rarr; <b>55 yellow</b> &rarr; <b>70 orange</b> &rarr; <b>82 red</b> &rarr; <b>90 magenta</b> &rarr; <b>HIGHEST+ 100 overcast</b> dark-purple. Same % always shows the same color; clear areas stay see-through. Satellite retrieval, not a weather model: no analysis blocks.</p><p><b>Source:</b> NOAA GOES-East (GOES-19) ABI L2 Clear Sky Mask, CONUS 2 km (5-minute scans)<br/><a href="https://www.goes-r.gov/products/baseline-clear-sky-mask">https://www.goes-r.gov/products/baseline-clear-sky-mask</a></p><p>Transparent outside valid water data so existing project layers (shipwrecks, lighthouses, harbors, parks) stay visible. Turn on/off independently of all other layers.</p><p><i>Not endorsed by NOAA.</i></p>]]></description>
    <Folder>
      <name>LIVE CLOUD COVER</name>
      <description><![CDATA[<h2>LIVE CLOUD COVER</h2><p>Observed cloud cover right now from the GOES-East weather satellite: the share of 2 km satellite pixels flagged cloudy around each point. Clear areas are transparent so the map underneath shows through. A direct satellite retrieval — not a weather-model estimate, so no analysis blocks.</p><p><img src="https://wyattleathorn7.github.io/great-lakes-live-environment/cloud_cover/legend.png?v=goes19-acmc-20260926-1821" width="600" alt="key"></p><p>Cloud cover (%, OBSERVED neighborhood fraction from GOES-East: share of 2 km satellite pixels flagged cloudy around each point): <b>LOWEST 0 clear</b> transparent &rarr; thin cloud <b>dark-blue/blue/cyan</b> &rarr; <b>40 green</b> &rarr; <b>55 yellow</b> &rarr; <b>70 orange</b> &rarr; <b>82 red</b> &rarr; <b>90 magenta</b> &rarr; <b>HIGHEST+ 100 overcast</b> dark-purple. Same % always shows the same color; clear areas stay see-through. Satellite retrieval, not a weather model: no analysis blocks.</p><p><b>Variable:</b> BCM binary mask (0 = clear_or_probably_clear, 1 = cloudy_or_probably_cloudy) gated by DQF==0; % = observed cloudy fraction per canvas neighborhood<br/><b>Units:</b> % cloud cover (observed)<br/><b>Source:</b> NOAA GOES-East (GOES-19) ABI L2 Clear Sky Mask, CONUS 2 km (5-minute scans)<br/><b>Update:</b> GOES-East 5-minute scans<br/><b>Data time:</b> 2026-09-26 18:21 UTC<br/><b>Source version:</b> goes19-acmc-20260926-1821<br/><b>Processed:</b> 2026-09-26 02:27 PM EDT<br/><b>Provenance:</b> <a href="https://www.goes-r.gov/products/baseline-clear-sky-mask">NOAA GOES</a></p>]]></description>
